  "behavior": [
    "Ownership/payload stable across waits; loser receives no stray acknowledgment.",
    "Fresh SETUP before every ACCESS; round-robin tie preference after idle.",
    "READY/error/read-data go only to owner; immediate withdrawal and reset cancel unfinished request.",
    "CPU and PCIe parked completed requests cannot be recaptured. PSEL-continuous new SETUP correctly rearms."
  ],
  "retained_history": "Initial copy happened after root applied the served fix and passed; it is not an unfixed-failure artifact. Actual guard-removal mutants demonstrate the reported defect. Initial five-case suite missed immediate PSEL-withdrawal and idle tie-preference mutants; final explicit checks reject both, with initial logs retained.",
  "boundaries": [
    "Port-only RTL and actual385-cell IHP mapped functional replay, no SDF/timing closure.",
    "Root separately owns full SoC CPU+PCIe/GPIO integration validation.",
    "Unmodified model timing-check warnings and cocotb executable-path diagnostic are retained, no timing-check execution claimed.",
    "No formal exhaustive proof, CDC or address policy is inferred from the arbiter alone."
  ],
